      "content": "We now move on to the partial derivatives of the log-likelihood required for the derivation of the ML estimators. Consider first the derivative with respect to the vector of fixed effects, $ \\beta $. This derivative involves only the final term of Equation 27.7b, and its procurement is facilitated by using a general result for matrix derivatives. Applying Equation A3.25d,",
